PE 843: Periodic Circles / 周期圆

=== Problem Interpretation ===
'Periodic Circles' involves circles arranged in a
periodic pattern, such as Ford circles, circle packings,
or lattice-based circle arrangements.

=== Ford Circles ===
Ford circle C(p,q): center (p/q, 1/(2q²)), radius 1/(2q²)
These circles are tangent or disjoint.

Examples (q ≤ 5):
  C(0/1): r = 0.500000, center = (0.000000, 0.500000)
  C(1/1): r = 0.500000, center = (1.000000, 0.500000)
  C(1/2): r = 0.125000, center = (0.500000, 0.125000)
  C(1/3): r = 0.055556, center = (0.333333, 0.055556)
  C(2/3): r = 0.055556, center = (0.666667, 0.055556)
  C(1/4): r = 0.031250, center = (0.250000, 0.031250)
  C(3/4): r = 0.031250, center = (0.750000, 0.031250)
  C(1/5): r = 0.020000, center = (0.200000, 0.020000)
  C(2/5): r = 0.020000, center = (0.400000, 0.020000)
  C(3/5): r = 0.020000, center = (0.600000, 0.020000)
  C(4/5): r = 0.020000, center = (0.800000, 0.020000)

=== Ford Circle Areas ===
  Total area (q ≤ 5): 0.8650405673
  Total area (q ≤ 10): 0.8700146712
  Total area (q ≤ 20): 0.8717183514

=== Periodic Circle Counting ===
Lattice points in circle of radius R (Gauss circle):
  R=1: N(R) = 5 (πR² ≈ 3.1)
  R=2: N(R) = 13 (πR² ≈ 12.6)
  R=3: N(R) = 29 (πR² ≈ 28.3)
  R=5: N(R) = 81 (πR² ≈ 78.5)
  R=10: N(R) = 317 (πR² ≈ 314.2)

